{
  "abstract": "We present a conditional Theta-closure realization relating Standard Model gauge couplings to internal geometric overlap integrals. Measured source data are transported with SMDR v1.3 into the full-Standard-Model modified minimal subtraction scheme at the top-mass matching scale. The profile targets are I2/I1 = 0.5110273 plus or minus 0.0001231 and I3/I1 = 0.158335 plus or minus 0.001098. These are calibrated profile coordinates, not first-principles gauge-coupling predictions. We formulate the admissibility and spectral-gap conditions under which an internal realization may reproduce them. A high-coherence twistor corner introduces declared period and gauge-kinetic normalizations for nonabelian harmonics. An overlap error estimate inversely proportional to the gap requires explicit projector and representative perturbation bounds. The top-mass matching scale is a renormalization convention, not a physical coherence, gap, or quantum-gravity scale. The result is a calibrated target and conditional existence test; independent geometric selection remains open.",
